\ KERNEL.SEQ    Load the F-PC kernel onto the VM's seed.   F-PC native port

\ This replaces META86.SEQ's load list (kernel-design.md 4.3): the C seed
\ FLOADs the kernel source in the original order; the kernel's own words
\ shadow the seed's as they are defined. INCLUDE is the seed's FLOAD:
\ the kernel defines its own FLOAD (FPATH.SEQ) before it can run it.

WARNING OFF
DECIMAL

INCLUDE KERNEL1.SEQ
INCLUDE VIDEO.SEQ
INCLUDE KERNEL2.SEQ
INCLUDE VIDEO2.SEQ
INCLUDE KERNEL3.SEQ
' SEED-ERROR IS ?ERROR          \ report errors to the seed until COLD
INCLUDE EXPAND.SEQ
INCLUDE EMMEXEC.SEQ
INCLUDE POINTER.SEQ
INCLUDE EQUCOLON.SEQ
INCLUDE SAVEREST.SEQ
INCLUDE HANDLES.SEQ
INCLUDE SEQREAD.SEQ
' SEED-ERROR IS ?ERROR
INCLUDE FPATH.SEQ
INCLUDE DEFAULT.SEQ
INCLUDE HCRITICA.SEQ
INCLUDE KERNEL4.SEQ

' (?SERROR) IS ?ERROR           \ F-PC's own error handling from now on

SEED-FILES CONSTANT KERNEL-FILES        \ where each kernel file's words are,
                                        \ for VIEW (VIEW.SEQ)

WARNING ON
